From: Ethan Hill <ethan.hill1999@outlook.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 14:46:46 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 29/30] KitKat UI P21: roll back the notification shade and
 quick settings to stock

User direction 2026-10-22: the shade/QS port did not feel good; both
surfaces ship stock LineageOS now. Everything else (status bar incl.
the 4.4 ticker, navbar, recents, keyguard, volume, power menu,
screenshot overlay, framework theme/fonts/sounds, app ports) stays.

Every shade/QS-only file is restored byte-identical to the LineageOS
baseline 993528cf0efb (= lineageos/lineage-21.0 tip): the P3 shade
items, P4 QS items, 11.1/11.2, P12 deep-port, P15 wholesale port,
P18 shade/QS parts, P20 donor rebuild, and the 12.6 core notification
typography (18sp/20sp titles back to stock). Shared files keep the
non-shade work (25dp status bar, ticker wiring, keyguard accent,
KitKatRecentsTheme, volume rail, power menu palette).

Verified: index diff vs baseline empty for all shade/QS files; no
dangling references to deleted KitKat shade/QS resources/classes;
m SystemUI (4:17) and m framework-res green on emu64x.

Superseded phases are marked in TASKS.md; the corrupted file tail
(spliced P20 duplicates) is replaced by the Phase 21 record.
